{
  "category": "Long Nose Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "It swings its long snout around playfully, but because it is so strong, that can be dangerous.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "As a sign of affection, it bumps with its snout. However, it is so strong, it may send you flying.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "During the deserted morning hours, it comes ashore where it deftly uses its trunk to take a shower.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "For its nest, PHANPY digs a vertical pit in the ground at the edge of a river. It marks the area around its nest with its trunk to let the others know that the area has been claimed.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "PHANPY uses its long nose to shower itself. When others gather around, they thoroughly douse each other with water. These POKéMON can be seen drying their soaking-wet bodies at the edge of water.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "PHANPY’s big ears serve as broad fans. When it becomes hot, it flaps the ears busily to cool down. Even the young are very strong.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "As a sign of affection, it bumps with its snout. However, it is so strong, it may send you flying.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "It swings its long snout around playfully, but because it is so strong, this can be dangerous.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is strong despite its compact size. It can easily pick up and carry an adult human on its back.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
